#: ../../installation.rst:2
msgid "Installation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../installation.rst:5
msgid "Download a release"
msgstr ""

#: ../../installation.rst:7
msgid ""
"Prebuilt packages are published on the `releases page "
"<https://github.com/jikhanjung/PaperMeister/releases>`_ for every tagged "
"version, with SHA256 checksums."
msgstr ""

#: ../../installation.rst:11
msgid "Windows"
msgstr ""

#: ../../installation.rst:12
msgid ""
"Download the portable ``.zip`` and run ``PaperMeister.exe`` from the "
"extracted folder, or use the installer (``.exe``) for a per-user install."
msgstr ""

#: ../../installation.rst:15
msgid "Linux"
msgstr ""

#: ../../installation.rst:16
msgid "Download the ``.AppImage``, make it executable (``chmod +x``) and run it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../installation.rst:18
msgid "macOS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../installation.rst:19
msgid ""
"Download the ``.dmg`` and drag the app to Applications. The build is "
"**not notarized**, so on first launch use Right-click → Open to get past "
"Gatekeeper."
msgstr ""

#: ../../installation.rst:22
msgid ""
"Windows is the best-tested platform; the Linux and macOS builds are "
"produced by CI but see less use."
msgstr ""

#: ../../installation.rst:26
msgid "Run from source"
msgstr ""

#: ../../installation.rst:35
msgid ""
"Python 3.12 or newer is required. For a reproducible environment matching"
" CI, install from the hash-pinned lockfile instead:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../installation.rst:42
msgid "Two other entry points share the same database:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../installation.rst:50
msgid "First run"
msgstr ""

#: ../../installation.rst:52
msgid ""
"Open **Settings** from the left rail and fill in what you need. Nothing "
"is required to browse, but each feature needs its own credentials."
msgstr ""

#: ../../installation.rst:55
msgid "Zotero"
msgstr ""

#: ../../installation.rst:56
msgid ""
"``user_id`` and an API key from https://www.zotero.org/settings/keys. A "
"read-only key is enough unless you want write-back, which needs write "
"permission on the library."
msgstr ""

#: ../../installation.rst:60
msgid "OCR"
msgstr ""

#: ../../installation.rst:61
msgid ""
"The URL (and key, if applicable) of your OCR backend. Three are "
"supported: RunPod serverless, a direct vLLM pod, and the wrapper API."
msgstr ""

#: ../../installation.rst:64
msgid "Bibliographic extraction"
msgstr ""

#: ../../installation.rst:65
msgid ""
"Choose the LLM backend — Claude via the ``claude`` CLI, or Qwen on your "
"own server. Automatic and manual extraction are separate toggles."
msgstr ""

#: ../../installation.rst:68
msgid ""
"Settings are written to ``~/.papermeister/preferences.json``. It holds "
"API keys in plain text, so treat it like any other credentials file."
msgstr ""

